Relevant columns and how they will be used  

• `stations.usaf`/`stations.wban` : primary keys of every weather station – used to join with the daily files.  
• `stations.lat`, `stations.lon`  : geographic coordinates – used in ST_DWITHIN to keep only stations ≤ 20 miles (≈ 32 186.8 m) from Chappaqua (41.197, ‑73.764).  
• `stations.name`        : human‑readable station name – returned in the final list.  
• `gsod20YY.stn`, `gsod20YY.wban` : station identifiers inside each annual GSOD table – joined to `stations`.  
• `gsod20YY.temp`        : daily mean temperature; rows with the sentinel value 9999.9 are thrown away (`WHERE temp != 9999.9`).  
• `gsod20YY.count_temp`     : quality check – optional extra filter (`count_temp > 0`).  
• `gsod20YY.year`, `mo`, `da`  : date parts – the tables we union already correspond to the proper years (2011‑2020).  

General conditions that will appear  

1. Geographic filter  
   `ST_DWITHIN( ST_GEOGPOINT(stations.lon, stations.lat),  
                ST_GEOGPOINT(-73.764, 41.197),  
                32186.8 )`    -- 20 miles in meters  
2. Valid temperature rows  
   `temp != 9999.9`   (and optionally `count_temp > 0`)  

Below are ten progressively more complex exploration queries (all limited to 20 rows).  
Replace or remove the LIMIT when you want the full result set.

```sql
-- 1. List the 20 stations closest to Chappaqua
SELECT usaf, wban, name, lat, lon,
       ST_DISTANCE(ST_GEOGPOINT(lon,lat),
                   ST_GEOGPOINT(-73.764,41.197)) AS meters_away
FROM `bigquery-public-data.noaa_gsod.stations`
ORDER BY meters_away
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 2. Count how many stations fall inside the 20‑mile radius
SELECT COUNT(*) AS stations_within_20_mi
FROM `bigquery-public-data.noaa_gsod.stations`
WHERE ST_DWITHIN(ST_GEOGPOINT(lon,lat),
                 ST_GEOGPOINT(-73.764,41.197),32186.8);
```

```sql
-- 3. Show identifiers of those nearby stations
SELECT usaf, wban, name
FROM `bigquery-public-data.noaa_gsod.stations`
WHERE ST_DWITHIN(ST_GEOGPOINT(lon,lat),
                 ST_GEOGPOINT(-73.764,41.197),32186.8)
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 4. Inspect one year (2011) – valid temperature rows for nearby stations
SELECT g.stn AS usaf, g.wban, g.temp
FROM `bigquery-public-data.noaa_gsod.gsod2011` AS g
JOIN `bigquery-public-data.noaa_gsod.stations` AS s
  ON g.stn = s.usaf AND g.wban = s.wban
WHERE ST_DWITHIN(ST_GEOGPOINT(s.lon,s.lat),
                 ST_GEOGPOINT(-73.764,41.197),32186.8)
  AND g.temp != 9999.9
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 5. Daily record counts in 2011 for each nearby station
SELECT g.stn AS usaf, g.wban, COUNT(*) AS valid_days_2011
FROM `bigquery-public-data.noaa_gsod.gsod2011` AS g
JOIN `bigquery-public-data.noaa_gsod.stations` AS s
  ON g.stn = s.usaf AND g.wban = s.wban
WHERE ST_DWITHIN(ST_GEOGPOINT(s.lon,s.lat),
                 ST_GEOGPOINT(-73.764,41.197),32186.8)
  AND g.temp != 9999.9
GROUP BY usaf, wban
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 6. Build a UNION of two sample years (2011‑2012) to preview multi‑year combining
SELECT g.stn AS usaf, g.wban, g.year
FROM (
      SELECT * FROM `bigquery-public-data.noaa_gsod.gsod2011`
      UNION ALL
      SELECT * FROM `bigquery-public-data.noaa_gsod.gsod2012`
     ) AS g
JOIN `bigquery-public-data.noaa_gsod.stations` AS s
  ON g.stn = s.usaf AND g.wban = s.wban
WHERE ST_DWITHIN(ST_GEOGPOINT(s.lon,s.lat),
                 ST_GEOGPOINT(-73.764,41.197),32186.8)
  AND g.temp != 9999.9
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 7. Year‑by‑year valid‑day counts, 2011‑2020
SELECT g.year, s.usaf, s.wban, s.name, COUNT(*) AS valid_days
FROM (
      -- one sub‑SELECT per year (abbreviated here with two; extend to 2020)
      SELECT * FROM `bigquery-public-data.noaa_gsod.gsod2011`
      UNION ALL SELECT * FROM `bigquery-public-data.noaa_gsod.gsod2012`
      UNION ALL SELECT * FROM `bigquery-public-data.noaa_gsod.gsod2013`
      UNION ALL SELECT * FROM `bigquery-public-data.noaa_gsod.gsod2014`
      UNION ALL SELECT * FROM `bigquery-public-data.noaa_gsod.gsod2015`
      UNION ALL SELECT * FROM `bigquery-public-data.noaa_gsod.gsod2016`
      UNION ALL SELECT * FROM `bigquery-public-data.noaa_gsod.gsod2017`
      UNION ALL SELECT * FROM `bigquery-public-data.noaa_gsod.gsod2018`
      UNION ALL SELECT * FROM `bigquery-public-data.noaa_gsod.gsod2019`
      UNION ALL SELECT * FROM `bigquery-public-data.noaa_gsod.gsod2020`
     ) AS g
JOIN `bigquery-public-data.noaa_gsod.stations` AS s
 ON g.stn = s.usaf AND g.wban = s.wban
WHERE ST_DWITHIN(ST_GEOGPOINT(s.lon,s.lat),
                 ST_GEOGPOINT(-73.764,41.197),32186.8)
  AND g.temp != 9999.9
GROUP BY g.year, s.usaf, s.wban, s.name
ORDER BY s.usaf, g.year
LIMIT 20;
